HST Office: a foreign OLE object that cannot be opened says why, in plain words (MathType formulas).

Double-clicking an embedded Windows OLE object whose program is not available (a MathType formula on a PC
without MathType, any such object on Linux and macOS) showed "Lỗi OLE chung khi kích hoạt đối tượng" (General
OLE error activating object). SfxInPlaceClient::DoVerb now shows an information box instead for that case
(an XEmbeddedOleObject failing with ERRCODE_SO_GENERALERROR): the program that made the object is not
installed or the system cannot run Windows OLE objects, and the object still shows and prints as it is. Other
errors and own objects (formulas, charts) keep the usual error box; the technical detail is logged.

